{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ef7e39d99b57bc5aee", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Electromagnetic Induction - Test 1", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264da9"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d64", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264cfc", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e0"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f9257"], "question": {"text": "<p>The induced emf can be produced in a coil by</p><p>A. moving the coil with uniform speed inside uniform magnetic field</p><p>B. moving the coil with non uniform speed inside uniform magnetic field</p><p>C. rotating the coil inside the uniform magnetic field</p><p>D. changing the area of the coil inside the uniform magnetic field</p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "7a677c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264cfd"}, {"id": "cb3c8a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264cfe"}, {"id": "bcf01b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi></math> only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264cff"}, {"id": "5cc1b5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d00"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d01", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b566e"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5644"], "question": {"text": "A coil is placed in a time varying magnetic field. If the number of turns in the coil were to be halved and the radius of wire doubled, the electrical power dissipated due to the current induced in the coil would be (Assume the coil to be short circuited.)"}, "options": [{"id": "5364f7", "text": "Doubled", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d02"}, {"id": "dd3961", "text": "The same", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d03"}, {"id": "921906", "text": "Quadrupled", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d04"}, {"id": "ce3fac", "text": "Halved", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d05"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d06", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b89"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95c4"], "question": {"text": "The figure shows a square loop <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> of side <math><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> which is connected to a network of resistances. The whole setup is moving towards the right with a constant speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> . At some instant, a part of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> is in a uniform magnetic field of&nbsp;<math><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>&nbsp;perpendicular to the plane of the loop. If the resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> is <math><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the current in the loop at that instant will be close to:<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F2b456b23-cb2d-4c38-abba-9dfb52cac127-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 419px; height: 175px;\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "38a6f1", "text": "<math><mn>115</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d07"}, {"id": "98b562", "text": "<math><mn>60</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d08"}, {"id": "989ce5", "text": "<math><mn>150</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d09"}, {"id": "c484c0", "text": "<math><mn>170</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d0a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d0b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b18"], "question": {"text": "A small square loop of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> and one turn is placed inside a larger square loop of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> and one turn <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8811;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The two loops are coplanar with their centres coinciding. If a current&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> is passed in the square loop of side&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the coefficient of mutual inductance between the two loops is :"}, "options": [{"id": "865434", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d0c"}, {"id": "d8b3db", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d0d"}, {"id": "33083f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d0e"}, {"id": "bea841", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d0f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d10", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60ced5dc19d2aa2b78a3a76c"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ed4"], "question": {"text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F39fd6419-0eb4-4bad-8590-f252b87abb14.png?alt=media\" /><br />As shown in the figure, a battery of emf <math><mo>&#8712;</mo></math> is connected to an inductor <math><mi>L</mi></math> and resistance <math><mi>R</mi></math> in series. The switch is closed at <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The total charge that flows from the battery, between <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></math> ( <math><msub><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></math> is the time constant of the circuit) is:"}, "options": [{"id": "7f3cc2", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d11"}, {"id": "60d1ed", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d12"}, {"id": "fa63bf", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d13"}, {"id": "564ca6", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d14"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d15", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f87fe"], "concepts": ["6162fb3b6ed13040ec84c84c"], "question": {"text": "<p>The energy of an electromagnetic wave contained in a small volume oscillates with</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "4215de", "text": "Double the frequency of the wave", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d16"}, {"id": "ba6297", "text": "The frequency of the wave", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d17"}, {"id": "60c34b", "text": "Half the frequency of the wave", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d18"}, {"id": "3a62dc", "text": "Zero frequency", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d19"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d1a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b89"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b5c"], "question": {"text": "A coil of area A and N turns is rotating with angular velocity \\(\\omega\\) in a uniform magnetic field \\(\\vec{B}\\) about an axis perpendicular to \\(\\vec{B}\\). Magnetic flux \\(\\varphi\\) and induced \\(\\operatorname{emf} \\varepsilon\\) across it, at an instant when \\(\\vec{B}\\) is parallel to the plane of coil, are :"}, "options": [{"id": "e7d8d8", "text": "\\(\\varphi=\\mathrm{AB}, \\varepsilon=0\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d1b"}, {"id": "b5fa6a", "text": "\\(\\varphi=0, \\varepsilon=0\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d1c"}, {"id": "b10af9", "text": "\\(\\varphi=0, \\varepsilon=\\mathrm{NAB} \\omega\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d1d"}, {"id": "b282f5", "text": "\\(\\varphi=\\mathrm{AB}, \\varepsilon=\\mathrm{NAB} \\omega\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d1e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d1f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5e"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b564a"], "question": {"text": "In a coil, the current changes from $-2 \\mathrm{~A}$ to $+2 \\mathrm{~A}$ in $0.2 \\mathrm{~s}$ and induces an emf of $0.1 \\mathrm{~V}$. The self inductance of the coil is :"}, "options": [{"id": "f0ff77", "text": "$4 \\mathrm{mH}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d20"}, {"id": "cf1fb7", "text": "$1 \\mathrm{mH}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d21"}, {"id": "f93c25", "text": "$5 \\mathrm{mH}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d22"}, {"id": "ae89cd", "text": "$2.5 \\mathrm{mH}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d23"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d24", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e0"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8edd"], "question": {"text": "A coil is placed in a magnetic field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> as shown below :<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F70d5d857-d8e7-4199-b783-f39442e1730e-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 348px; height: 160px;\" /><br />A current is induced in the coil because <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> is :"}, "options": [{"id": "9184a2", "text": "parallel to the plane of coil and increasing with time", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d25"}, {"id": "8d4470", "text": "outward and increasing with time", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d26"}, {"id": "f1ce44", "text": "outward and decreasing with time", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d27"}, {"id": "ae95f0", "text": "parallel to the plane of coil and decreasing with time", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d28"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d29", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f87fe"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f924f"], "question": {"text": "<p>Two coils of self inductance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are connected in series combination having mutual inductance of the coils as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>. The equivalent self inductance of the combination will be</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F42385901-12f9-4eb9-80a7-9d42b05e90b4-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 69px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "68b4e0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d2a"}, {"id": "39c839", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d2b"}, {"id": "a6a576", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d2c"}, {"id": "334522", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d2d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d2e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60ced5dc19d2aa2b78a3a76c"], "concepts": ["60ced5db19d2aa2b78a3a740"], "question": {"text": "<p>The figure&nbsp;shows a circuit that contains four identical resistors with resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;two identical inductors with inductance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mH</mi></math> and an ideal battery with E.M.F.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi></math> just after the switch <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> is closed will be:</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fd4bc1cb7-998f-41b1-b6ed-24b00e700199-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 287px; height: 144px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "2c9ae2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d2f"}, {"id": "861fd7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>37</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d30"}, {"id": "1792a3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d31"}, {"id": "f4d31c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d32"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d33", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b566e"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5644"], "question": {"text": "A rectangular metallic loop is moving out of a uniform magnetic field region to a field free region with a constant speed. When the loop is partially inside the magnate field, the plot of magnitude of induced emf $(\\varepsilon)$ with time $(t)$ is given by"}, "options": [{"id": "168058", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FY9TtPaGnAAY_L86pujzws5V_CW1SlymGcLv2waeMtxw.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d34"}, {"id": "7d12d4", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FL8-8fUEkdr6fH1PSfA8GHjV1UoqP6ji8xR6TV0q8hRs.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d35"}, {"id": "8cb614", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F7ToJqUwk4u-YAfIRWg2kvoV5cUmrTz_I9P_ZaXbAMNk.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d36"}, {"id": "980182", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fw5w0mwTKHWcvIwpdvtVhL2Htfxn-MSSBNOYVxQZ75bw.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d37"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d38", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e0"], "concepts": ["60ced5db19d2aa2b78a3a73a"], "question": {"text": "Consider a circular coil of wire carrying constant current <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> forming a magnetic dipole. The magnetic flux through an infinite plane that contains the circular coil and excluding the circular coil area is given by <math><msub><mrow><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></math> The magnetic flux through the area of the circular coil area is given by <math><msub><mrow><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> . Which of the following option is correct?"}, "options": [{"id": "30557a", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d39"}, {"id": "b787ec", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d3a"}, {"id": "f13e64", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d3b"}, {"id": "718dd3", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d3c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d3d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f87fe"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87ce"], "question": {"text": "The self induced emf of a coil is <math><mn>25</mn></math> volts. When the current in it is changed at uniform rate from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> , the change in the energy of the inductance is:"}, "options": [{"id": "49a348", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>637.5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d3e"}, {"id": "7c3cec", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>740</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d3f"}, {"id": "db72dc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>437.5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d40"}, {"id": "cd2a4e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>540</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d41"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d42", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b89"], "concepts": ["6162fb386ed13040ec84c686"], "question": {"text": "A thin strip <math><mn>10</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> long is on a <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi></math> shaped wire of negligible resistance and it is connected to a spring of spring constant <math><mn>0.5</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> (see figure). The assembly is kept in a uniform magnetic field of <math><mn>0.1</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the strip is pulled from its equilibrium position and released, the number of oscillations it performs before its amplitude decreases by a factor of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></math> is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> . If the mass of the strip is <math><mn>50</mn></math> grams, its resistance <math><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> and air drag negligible, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> will be close to:<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fd72e34f8-3dd4-4ae5-a09d-1dacd793ddec-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 260px; height: 148px;\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "064d27", "text": "<math><mi> </mi><mn>1000</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d43"}, {"id": "92daf5", "text": "<math><mn>5000</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d44"}, {"id": "d5e945", "text": "<math><mn>10000</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d45"}, {"id": "15ca26", "text": "<math><mn>50000</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d46"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d47", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b18"], "question": {"text": "Two conducting circular loops A and B are placed in the same plane with their centers coinciding as shown in figure. The mutual inductance between them is :\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FU36tbNPWw38Nzax4Rfn2XC_gLMAfxmx0q-nyFveJwNc.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "3ef53f", "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_0 \\pi b^2}{2 a}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d48"}, {"id": "58a531", "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_o}{2 \\pi} \\cdot \\frac{b^2}{a}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d49"}, {"id": "3dfd31", "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_0}{2 \\pi} \\cdot \\frac{a^2}{b}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d4a"}, {"id": "fc8f8e", "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_0 \\pi a^2}{2 b}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d4b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d4c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60ced5dc19d2aa2b78a3a76c"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ed4"], "question": {"text": "An emf of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> is applied at time <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> to a circuit containing in series <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> inductor and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>&#937;</mtext></math> resistor. The ratio of the currents at time <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#8734;</mi></math> and at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>s</mtext></math> is close to: (Take <math><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>7.389</mn></math> )"}, "options": [{"id": "e9507a", "text": "<math><mn>1.06</mn></math>", "isCorrec