L\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> directed along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math>- axis. In equilibrium the potential difference between the faces of higher and lower potential developed because of the motion through the field will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mV</mi></math>.<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fc6bd4656-663d-4ee0-b29f-217ce50b89d9.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 301px;\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "23aa61", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d8f"}, {"id": "fd4441", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d90"}, {"id": "16219c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d91"}, {"id": "23e45d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d92"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d93", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5e"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b564a"], "question": {"text": "The current in a coil of self inductance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> is increasing according to the law <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced></math>. Find the amount of energy spent (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>) during the period when the current changes from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "0ba7a7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d94"}, {"id": "5a3775", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d95"}, {"id": "ac5322", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d96"}, {"id": "89f614", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d97"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d98", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60ced5dc19d2aa2b78a3a76c"], "concepts": ["60ced5db19d2aa2b78a3a740"], "question": {"text": "<p>A part of a complete circuit is shown in the figure. At some instant, the value of current I is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and it is decreasing at a rate of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>As</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of the potential difference&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></math> (in volts) at that instant is-</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F0f376ace-ca8a-484d-95f7-14e61169edf3-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 95px;\" />&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "a4c0a5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d99"}, {"id": "bc78ec", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d9a"}, {"id": "2f251c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d9b"}, {"id": "25f6c3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d9c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4c2ee0e063d9264d9d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfadf"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f87fe"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87ce"], "question": {"text": "<p>Consider an electrical circuit containing a two way switch <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Initially <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> is open and then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is connected to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;As the current in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> attains a maximum value of steady-state level, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is disconnected from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and immediately connected to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Potential drop across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> resistor immediately after <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is connected to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>.</mo></math> (Round off to the Nearest Integer)</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fc4ff0db2-b9a5-4e4c-ad8e-6bd96d2198c3-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 139px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "a0b89f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69d